  "title": "Model health became part of discovery",
  "summary": "Model discovery became more honest about reliability while agents, new models, and community-built tools gave people more to do with the catalog.\n\nReliability moved from a behind-the-scenes check into model listings and tools for inspecting routes. Enter now starts with healthy official models, list requests can filter by health, and listings include a 24-hour health signal by default. Separate status and route views show when a fallback rescued a request—and when the primary route still needs attention. Models without measurements report `unknown`.\n\nEndpoint agents can declare their input and output modalities, accept request metadata across three API surfaces, and use an inner-model override in Chat Completions. Computer MCP agents gained shared public memory, more shell and Git tools, and commits attributed by default to the caller’s linked GitHub identity. Two one-time Quests reward trying an eligible agent or creating one that receives a successful request.\n\nElevenLabs Music v2.5 brought 3–300-second music generation; paid-only FLUX.2 Max added image generation and editing with up to eight reference images. GPT-4o Mini and two Tencent reasoning models joined the paid-only text lineup, while Jev added typed decisions from JSON state. Llama 4 Scout returned with updated routing and a narrower declared capability set, which requests now check up front.\n\nPollinations chat models gained a provider for Simon Willison’s `llm` CLI and Python library. The `polli` CLI gained an opt-in update command and more useful usage filters, token totals, and CSV export. Reusable React chat components, inline dashboard media, and Copy buttons for code blocks made the surrounding tools less fiddly.",
  "pr_count": 100,
